.SH NAME

jogtranslator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.HP
.B loadrt jogtranslator [count=\fIN\fB|names=\fIname1\fB[,\fIname2...\fB]]
.SH DESCRIPTION

Pre-compute g_multiplier as sixth-root on max_speed/min_speed
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
\fBjogtranslator.\fIN\fB\fR (requires a floating-point thread)
This comp translates raw data from shuttle devices to drive jogging pins
.SH PINS
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-butt-0\fR bit in \fR
TRUE if button 0 pressed
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-butt-1\fR bit in \fR
TRUE if button 1 pressed
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-butt-2\fR bit in \fR
TRUE if button 2 pressed
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-butt-3\fR bit in \fR
TRUE if button 3 pressed
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-butt-4\fR bit in \fR
TRUE if button 4 pressed
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ring-raw\fR s32 in \fR
Signed value of jog ring position
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.min-speed\fR float in \fR
Minimum output value i.e. wheel in position 1
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.g-multiplier\fR float in \fR
Max output value for position 7 is min_speed * g_multiplier^6
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.radio-latching\fR u32 in \fR
Set true if you want the priority ax_butt signals to be latched
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-0-pos\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 0 in positive direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-0-neg\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 0 in negative direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-0-sel\fR bit out \fR
Axis 0 is selected
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-1-pos\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 1 in positive direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-1-neg\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 1 in negative direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-1-sel\fR bit out \fR
Axis 1 is selected
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-2-pos\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 2 in positive direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-2-neg\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 2 in negative direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-2-sel\fR bit out \fR
Axis 2 is selected
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-3-pos\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 3 in positive direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-3-neg\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 3 in negative direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-3-sel\fR bit out \fR
Axis 3 is selected
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-4-pos\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 4 in positive direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-4-neg\fR bit out \fR
Jog axis 4 in negative direction
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-out-4-sel\fR bit out \fR
Axis 4 is selected
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-selected-axis\fR s32 out \fR
Number of selected axis or -1 if none
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.ax-jog-speed\fR float out \fR
Translated jogging speed
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.smallest-step\fR float in \fR
Value of the smallest jogging step e.g. 0.001
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.number-of-stepsizes\fR u32 in \fR
Count of different stepsizes to be generated
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.cycle-stepsizes\fR bit in \fR
moves to next size of step when this goes high. Wraps around in hitting number if sizes
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.jog-microstep-size\fR float out \fR
Size of desired step divided by 1000 as each wheel click is 1000 microsteps
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.shuttle-step-index\fR u32 out \fR
Index to hal table of step sizes - smallest is 0 up to number_of_stepsizes - 1
.TP
.B jogtranslator.\fIN\fB.gui-step-index\fR u32 in \fR
Channel from GUI to hal table of step sizes - smallest is 0 up to number_of_stepsizes - 1
